        <nav class="breadcrumb reveal"><a href="index.html">Home</a> / <a href="uganda.html">Uganda</a> / Jinja &amp; the Nile</nav>

        <p class="article__lead reveal">It was here, at Jinja, that explorers finally pinpointed the source of the Nile, the spot where Lake Victoria spills north on a 6,600 kilometre journey to the Mediterranean. Today the river makes Jinja East Africa's adventure capital, from heart pounding white water to a gentle sunset float.</p>

        <h2 class="reveal">Why visit Jinja?</h2>
        <p class="reveal">A relaxed riverside town a couple of hours east of Kampala, Jinja blends history, adventure and easy charm. Whether you want adrenaline or simply to stand where two great explorers once stood, it's a wonderful change of pace, and a fun, accessible add on at the start or end of a Uganda journey.</p>

        <h2 class="reveal">The source of the Nile</h2>
        <p class="reveal">A boat trip to the source is a quiet thrill: your guide points out where the lake water visibly wells up to begin the river, with a marker for the spot where Speke confirmed the source in 1862. It's a low key but genuinely moving moment, the beginning of the longest river on earth.</p>

        <h2 class="reveal">Things to do</h2>
        <ul class="reveal">
          <li><strong>White water rafting:</strong> world class grade five rapids for the brave, with calmer family floats too.</li>
          <li><strong>On the water:</strong> kayaking, stand up paddleboarding and serene sunset cruises.</li>
          <li><strong>On land:</strong> quad biking, mountain biking, and visits to local craft and community projects.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="reveal">Best time to visit</h2>
        <p class="reveal">Jinja is enjoyable year round; the river runs regardless of season. The drier months, <strong>June to September</strong> and <strong>December to February</strong>, are most comfortable for time on the water. See our <a href="best-time-uganda.html">best time to visit Uganda</a> guide for more.</p>

        <h2 class="reveal">Where to stay &amp; how to get there</h2>
        <p class="reveal">We favour lodges set in gardens right above the river, with the sound of the rapids below. Jinja is an easy drive from Entebbe or Kampala, making it a natural first or last stop, and a brilliant, gentle adventure for families on our <a href="uganda-family-adventure.html">Uganda Family Adventure</a>. We arrange every transfer.</p>

